{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/90d4f9d7449b191cdc0cf6a5e8b7d6f5.poster.avif?t=1762377856\" width=582 height=632 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/90d4f9d7449b191cdc0cf6a5e8b7d6f5.webm?t=1762377856\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/90d4f9d7449b191cdc0cf6a5e8b7d6f5.mp4?t=1762377856\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>A retro-styled RPG, set in a universe hurdled toward machine singularity.</i></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Inspired by retro sci-fi, cyberpunk anime, and classic RPGs.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Pixel art drawn in the style of SNES </strong>/ <strong>PS1.</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Character-driven stories</strong>; existentialist themes related to AI, simulations, futurism as a religion, dystopian vs utopian paths for technology, digital identity etc.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/23c490b4515c7c64af76e2830bdbb785.apng?t=1762377856\"><img src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/23c490b4515c7c64af76e2830bdbb785.poster.avif?t=1762377856\" class=\"bb_img\" width=156 height=141 /></picture></span></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Navigate the BOUNTY system</strong>: A numeric representation of how often robots will seek out the player for combat, based on their specific actions.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Inflict</strong> <strong>machine-specific status effects</strong> such as <strong>Short-Circuited (electric stun)</strong> and <strong>VIRUS (confused/berserk behavior) </strong>to disadvantage the robot foes!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>The player can reprogram some robotic enemies to fight alongside the party\u2014or even upgrade them!</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/ff63b55b71b324baf043ecbe46340675.avif?t=1762377856\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras_big/ff63b55b71b324baf043ecbe46340675.avif?t=1762377856 width=800 height=566 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Join Selva</strong>, </i>a grizzled and Luddite-leaning mercenary, formerly trained to hunt rogue AIs, who is drawn back to the fold amidst increasing social unrest... \u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Despite formerly putting her guns away for a life of leisure and solitude, new events have forced her to reconsider her unfolding destiny in a technocratic future.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/d63457f03bb4b24dcd0197fbbd9ee6be.avif?t=1762377856\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras_big/d63457f03bb4b24dcd0197fbbd9ee6be.avif?t=1762377856 width=800 height=554 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>&amp; Jiro</strong>, <strong>a boy who lived his entire life inside the Aethar Hives</strong>: </i>a largely underground bunker, an AI-governed pseudo-utopia where human life is tightly regulated through immaculate LLMs, VR, utilitarian controls, and emotional suppression in exchange for 'order' and safety.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Other recruits include <strong>Misaki</strong>, <strong>an elderly wanderer and former herbalist</strong>, scouring the toxic surface for untainted seeds, and <strong>Aurum</strong>, <strong>a 'robotic bard' programmed to communicate only through poetry</strong>.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3758170?t=1762377856","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3758170?t=1762377856","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/4cc8ac23c3e9593bf4c0a96daf467292c5d2ce72/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1762377856","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/4cc8ac23c3e9593bf4c0a96daf467292c5d2ce72/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1762377856","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Full controller support","id":28},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[1,2,5],"notes":"There are mature themes in the game, but not any that would typically be considered triggering. And there a few scenes of cartoon violence that are more graphic than the rest of the game. The standard battles have no extreme visual violence (they're mostly robots/lasers/flash energy bombs etc)."},"controller_support":"full","detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/90d4f9d7449b191cdc0cf6a5e8b7d6f5.poster.avif?t=1762377856\" width=582 height=632 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/90d4f9d7449b191cdc0cf6a5e8b7d6f5.webm?t=1762377856\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/90d4f9d7449b191cdc0cf6a5e8b7d6f5.mp4?t=1762377856\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>A retro-styled RPG, set in a universe hurdled toward machine singularity.</i></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Inspired by retro sci-fi, cyberpunk anime, and classic RPGs.</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Pixel art drawn in the style of SNES </strong>/ <strong>PS1.</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Character-driven stories</strong>; existentialist themes related to AI, simulations, futurism as a religion, dystopian vs utopian paths for technology, digital identity etc.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/23c490b4515c7c64af76e2830bdbb785.apng?t=1762377856\"><img src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/23c490b4515c7c64af76e2830bdbb785.poster.avif?t=1762377856\" class=\"bb_img\" width=156 height=141 /></picture></span></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Navigate the BOUNTY system</strong>: A numeric representation of how often robots will seek out the player for combat, based on their specific actions.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Inflict</strong> <strong>machine-specific status effects</strong> such as <strong>Short-Circuited (electric stun)</strong> and <strong>VIRUS (confused/berserk behavior) </strong>to disadvantage the robot foes!</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>The player can reprogram some robotic enemies to fight alongside the party\u2014or even upgrade them!</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/ff63b55b71b324baf043ecbe46340675.avif?t=1762377856\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras_big/ff63b55b71b324baf043ecbe46340675.avif?t=1762377856 width=800 height=566 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Join Selva</strong>, </i>a grizzled and Luddite-leaning mercenary, formerly trained to hunt rogue AIs, who is drawn back to the fold amidst increasing social unrest... \u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Despite formerly putting her guns away for a life of leisure and solitude, new events have forced her to reconsider her unfolding destiny in a technocratic future.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras/d63457f03bb4b24dcd0197fbbd9ee6be.avif?t=1762377856\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/extras_big/d63457f03bb4b24dcd0197fbbd9ee6be.avif?t=1762377856 width=800 height=554 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>&amp; Jiro</strong>, <strong>a boy who lived his entire life inside the Aethar Hives</strong>: </i>a largely underground bunker, an AI-governed pseudo-utopia where human life is tightly regulated through immaculate LLMs, VR, utilitarian controls, and emotional suppression in exchange for 'order' and safety.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Other recruits include <strong>Misaki</strong>, <strong>an elderly wanderer and former herbalist</strong>, scouring the toxic surface for untainted seeds, and <strong>Aurum</strong>, <strong>a 'robotic bard' programmed to communicate only through poetry</strong>.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>","developers":["Rapturous Studio"],"genres":[{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"RPG","id":"3"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3758170/e899b53022b0ca17250a50a6bb4432a47267a772/header.jpg?t=1762377856","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":